# Citation metadata for GLINT (Citation File Format 1.2.0). GitHub reads this file for "Cite this repository";
# DOE CODE and Zenodo read the same fields. Keep `version` equal to pyproject.toml's and fill `doi` and
# `date-released` when the DOE CODE record is announced at the tagged release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GLINT, please cite the method paper below and this software record."
type: software
title: "GLINT: a fast GPU-native blind crystallography indexer"
abstract: >-
  GLINT indexes sparse single-shot serial-crystallography diffraction blind, with no unit cell supplied, on the
  GPU: candidate lattices are generated per frame from a gridless objective, the weak but recurrent hypotheses
  are pooled across frames to identify a shared unit cell by cross-frame consensus, and each frame is then
  registered against that cell with a batched known-cell engine. It ingests what a CrystFEL or LUTE peak search
  emits and writes a CrystFEL stream, and it ships a device-resident streaming driver that discovers the cell
  while the data arrive.
authors:
  - family-names: Marchesini
    given-names: Stefano
    affiliation: "SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory"
    email: smarches@slac.stanford.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6798-2913"
  - family-names: Ni
    given-names: Yuan
    affiliation: "SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
# doi: 10.11578/dc.XXXXXXXX  (the DOE CODE DOI, when announced)
repository-code: "https://github.com/slac-lcls/glint"
# LICENSE.md is BSD-3-Clause plus the SLAC/DOE enhancements grant-back; no single SPDX identifier names that
# text exactly, so the file is referenced rather than an identifier asserted.
license-url: "https://github.com/slac-lcls/glint/blob/main/LICENSE.md"
keywords:
  - crystallography
  - serial crystallography
  - SFX
  - indexing
  - blind indexing
  - unit cell
  - consensus
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - diffraction
  - LCLS
  - XFEL
  - CrystFEL
